                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "**UPDATE**\nThe dev is working on the game, so bugs have been fixed. Yay! Now I just need to beat the hardest difficulties.\n\n**ORIGINAL**\nTo start off, I played a demo of this before I bought it, so my play time is actually a little more than Steam shows.\n\nSudokube is a new and challenging twist on the classic Sudoku. Spin a 4x4x4 cube to arrange 16 alphanumeric characters (standard hex values) across the faces of the cube without repeats across rows, columns, or faces.\n\nThe game is simple, and put together fairly well (doesn't require much), but I did hit a few snags/hangs where the cube wouldn't rotate until I restarted the game. This is not a high-end machine I was running on, and I was multitasking, so it's *probably* my fault. That being said, the game is still good!",
